      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. That makes sense. I'm also seeing a lot of these small, irregular inclusions in some of the darker bits, almost like little organic bits or grit that didn't melt quite right. Does the inclusion type or the way the shards are scattered/broken across the stratum give any clues about whether the vessels were manufactured in situ or if they were just debris being moved around by external factors?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
